        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "uQ4TZ",
          "x": 84,
          "y": 2680,
          "name": "S1 Notes",
          "fill": "$ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 6300,
          "content": "Notes on readings chosen:\n• Standing props sit on the ground line at 92% of frame height, centred on their ink. Glass vessels are outline only. back / front / shine share one coordinate set so they stack exactly.\n• vessel_bottle: \"330x720 body\" read as the lower 720 px of the vessel (shoulders included), neck 130 wide above it, lip ring at the mouth.\n• vessel_mug_shine: size not given, made 640x540 to register with vessel_mug_body. vessel_mug_opening: place its top-left at (32, 17) in body coordinates; its ring uses the body's line weights (the 90 px frame would give under 1 px).\n• \"Opaque\" read as a solid Ink object; the background stays transparent everywhere.\n• bench_table_top and bench_table_apron tile horizontally: planks run left-right (seams closer toward the back = the slight convergence), and the 2 px border is dropped on the left/right edges only, so the tile has no seam.\n• bench_table_end: side view along the table (end grain of the top, the apron's end, one turned leg to the floor). On the small frames (apron, leg) carved lines use Heavy-based widths so cuts stay 1.5-3 px wide.\n• The .pen format has no per-frame export setting: export each frame as PNG at 1x; frame names are the file names.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
