        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s2qxxxH",
          "x": 84,
          "y": 1652,
          "name": "Notes",
          "fill": "$ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 2800,
          "content": "• All pieces are solid Ink with carved (cut-out) lines; the game tints them. Transparent background everywhere.\n• fx_steam_1..3: the carved wind gusts stood on end. Tapered strokes rising in an S from a needle tip at the cup mouth (128, 507), thick low, thinning upward, rolling into thick spirals, breaking into dashes at the top. 1 = three side-by-side strokes (wind_gust_1), 2 = two staggered gusts, each rolling into a big curl (a strong boil), 3 = thin staggered wisps (cooling steam, wind_gust_3).\n• fx_bubbles_1..3: thin rings (about HEAVY), one highlight each, interior transparent. 1 = a rising column, 2 = a tight cluster (front bubbles hide the rings behind them), 3 = one big bubble plus a few small ones. They have 8, 8 and 6 bubbles.\n• fx_splash_1..3: side view on a flat liquid base at y = 372, impact point (256, 372). 1 = a crown of tapering tongues with beads and pinching drops, 2 = a rising jet with a drop pinching off above a low crown, 3 = liquid thrown sideways to the right (a sheet breaking into beaded fingers, with a small counter-splash to the left).\n• fx_drop_1..2: a falling teardrop with its highlight, glint and rim carved out. 2 is smaller and sits low in the frame, with a short broken trail above it.\n• fx_foam_1..2: bubbles packed on a flat base (y = 156, solid strip); bubbles in front are separated from those behind by a carved gap. The top bubbles are partly open rings, so the foam gets lighter toward the top. Tileable on x (the 2 px border is dropped on x); the seam was checked with two copies side by side. 2 is lower and finer, with loose bubbles above it.\n• fx_stain_1..2: a puddle drawn in plan with round scallops, then squashed to about 0.28 for the slant. It has a solid rim, a carved line just inside it, and broken horizontal sheen lines that are densest in a band a little above the centre. There are a few flattened outlier drops. 1 = one broad stain, 2 = a main pool running into a second, smaller pool.\n• Line weights: at these small frames FINE (and MEDIUM on S <= 256) is under 1.5 px, so the carved lines use HEAVY-based widths of 1.8 to 2.6 px. Splash uses MEDIUM 2.3 px, and its finest cut is 1.9 px.\n• Nothing was skipped. Bubbles from the earlier run were kept, with occlusion added in the cluster. The earlier steam was replaced because it read as plant stems.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
