          "content": "• All ink on transparent; the game tints it white-blue. No line or cut under ~1.5 px: the 128 px pieces (beads, trails, icicles) and the 160 px snow use Heavy-based widths (1.6 to 2.8 px) because Fine/Medium would fall under 1.5 px.\n• glass_ice_fern_1..4: fronds of frost with twigs at about 60 degrees toward the tip, shorter toward the tips, each twig carrying smaller twigs; fronds are lopsided (one side longer), as frost grows. 1 fans out of the bottom-left corner, 2 grows in from the right edge, 3 hangs from the top edge, 4 is a free six-armed snowflake with a small hexagonal plate (carved hexagon) at the centre.\n• glass_frost_veil (tiles both ways): the mist sits in drifting patches covering ~30% of the tile (a periodic noise above its 70th percentile, with a light sprinkle outside); inside them specks, short hairline scratches leaning mostly about -25 degrees, and a few tiny six-armed crystals.\n• glass_bead_1..3: lens-edge ring, ink highlight comma (and a speck) upper left, a dark crescent lower right with one slim carved arc in it. 1 small, 2 medium, 3 large and slightly flattened (wider than tall, a touch heavier at the bottom). Centred in the frame.\n• glass_trail_1..2: a clean channel down the mist: two thin broken edge lines, mist beads crowding just outside, two or three residue droplets inside, the same bead at the bottom with its rim open where the run enters. 1 starts inside the frame with a rounded start; 2 enters from the top edge and jogs sideways once.\n• glass_condensation (tiles both ways): ~520 very tiny beads; most are dots, the middle sizes are a ring that thickens into the lower-right crescent, a few larger ones get the bead ring, crescent and a speck of highlight. Density breathes with a periodic noise.\n• glass_sill_snow (tiles horizontally): solid ink heap, flat base on the bottom 2 px border line (y=158), scalloped top rolling in long periodic swells; carved crest gouges under each scallop, sparkle dots, broken drift layers. The top of the heap is 47 to ~110 px above the base.\n• glass_icicle_1..3: hang from a lumpy ridge of ice touching the top border; pointed icicles of different lengths with refrozen bulges, a carved highlight line down the left, short ring gouges on the right, a drop forming under the longest tip. 1 has 4 icicles (longest 345), 2 has 4 (longest 320), 3 has 5 (longest 300).\n• glass_dirt (tiles both ways): six round smudges (dried water spots: broken rims, inner wipe arcs, stipple crowding toward the rim), three partial fingerprints (nested loop ridges fading out on one side), five run streaks with a dried drip at the end, plus dust speck and a few nicks; the marks cover about 17% of the tile.\n• Seams checked by tiling the previews 2x2 (2x1 for the snow): no visible seam.\n• Nothing skipped.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
