          "content": "• Curtains: hang from 7 rings; ring centres at y=26 in the curtain frame, the rod's centre line at y=30 in room_curtain_rod, so place each curtain frame 4 px below the rod frame's top (curtain.y = rod.y + 4). Left and right are mirror images (outer edge straight, inner window edge swings in slightly at mid height) with different fold rhythms; scalloped hem, a diamond band above it. FINE at S=360 is 1.08 px, so fine cuts use 1.7 px (HEAVY-based minimum).\n• Rod: rod from x=96 to x=904 with turned finials outside; wall brackets at x=150 and x=850 rising to the top edge (wall plates).\n• Tieback: hook ring at the top (x=60, y=12), twisted cord loop, knot at y=100, tassel to y=190. Small frame: all lines use >=1.6 px.\n• Shutters: two louvred leaves (louvres = carved slat lines, a tilt bar), raised lower panels with a cordel diamond, strap hinges on the outer edges. Closed leaves fill x 8..452, y 24..696. Open = the same leaves swung INTO the room about their hinges (the outer edges stay at x=8 / x=452, same top/bottom there), foreshortened by a homography to 100 px wide; the free edges are nearer the viewer, so 3.5% taller (y 12..708), with the leaf thickness shown as a narrow edge face. The opening between the leaves is empty.\n• Rug: lies on the floor as a trapezoid (back edge y=36, front edge y=166, plus a 6 px thickness strip), fringe on both short ends. Not a standing prop, so no 92% ground rule.\n• Stove: OPAQUE solid silhouette with carved detail; plinth bottom on the 92% ground line (y=478.4), centred. Pot on the LEFT hob, right hob shown bare (concentric rings); stove pipe at the back right reaching y~4; firebox door with a horizontal air slot cut out, ash pit below, an arched niche of firewood under the right side. No fire drawn (the game lights it).\n• Shelf: a wall shelf (plank top y 196..210, scalloped trim to ~237, brackets to y=286). Items stand on y=203: clay jug (x~196, spout left, handle right), tin cup (x~356), tin candle holder with an UNLIT candle (x~520, wick tip ~y 76). Each item is set off from the plank by a 2 px carved gap.\n• Hanging lamp: ceiling plate at the top edge (y 3..11, the ceiling contact), hook, chain, crown ring y=148, smoke bell, glass chimney OUTLINE ONLY (y 206..332, centre x=120; its interior is transparent, flame anchor ~ (120, 300) just above the wick tip at y~302), burner gallery, font, drop finial to y~478. Unlit. MEDIUM/FINE at S=240 are under 1.5 px, so HEAVY-based widths (2.3 / 1.7 px) are used.\n• Nothing skipped.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
