        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s6qxxxR",
          "x": 84,
          "y": 2760,
          "name": "Notes",
          "fill": "$ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 3560,
          "content": "• All neutral solid ink, carving cut out as holes; transparent background; 2 px border kept (mud bank wraps on x).\n• pond_lilypad_1..3: flat round leaves seen at a slant (flattened ellipses), notch to the centre, carved radiating veins; 1 = one pad, 2 = two overlapping, 3 = a cluster of three. Lowest edge on the 92% line = the waterline.\n• pond_lily_flower: a water lily (ninfeia) floating, side view at a slant, rows of pointed petals separated by carved gaps, crown of stamens; base on the 92% line.\n• pond_reeds_1..3: reed blades + two cattail spikes, leaning slightly. Every blade/cattail is its own separate shape (min gap ~4 px, 8-10 shapes each) so the game can bend them one by one; bases on the 92% line (y 644), centred.\n• pond_stone_1..5: rounded stones (single, flat slab, pair, upright egg, group of three); light contour gouges on the upper left, a carved waterline near the base with a solid 'wet' band under it. Base on the 92% line.\n• pond_mud_bank: tileable horizontally (period 1920, seam checked: top edge at y 89 on both edges). Wavy muddy top edge, carved strata, embedded pebbles, a few stones sitting on the edge, footprints (bare human feet, heron tracks, capivara). Mud runs to the bottom of the frame (bottom 2 px border kept).\n• pond_fish_1..2: 1 = rising out of the water, head up, tail still at the surface with a splash crown; 2 = top of the leap, arched over, drops falling back along its path and rings where it left. Waterline = 92% line (lowest ink).\n• anim_dragonfly: one dragonfly (libélula) side view facing right, hovering; body identical in all four cells, only the wings move (fore/hind out of phase): 1 all up, 2 forewings level / hindwings up, 3 all down, 4 forewings rising / hindwings down; loops 4 -> 1. No ground line (it flies); same position in every cell. Wings are membrane outlines with carved veins (glass-like, interior open).\n• pond_leaf: a fallen leaf floating, flattened by the slant, short stem, carved midrib and side veins, near edge curling; lowest edge on the 92% line.\n• pond_rings_1..3: ripples as thin concentric flattened ellipses of broken carved lines, inner rings bolder; ring centre = frame centre (256, 96) for anchoring on a splash or the fish's re-entry point; 3 has a second small ring set overlapping (two drops).\n• Nothing missing: all 20 assets of S6 delivered.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
