        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s7qxxxZ",
          "x": 84,
          "y": 2732,
          "name": "Notes",
          "fill": "$ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 3392,
          "content": "• All neutral: solid Ink, every carved line cut out; no flame, glow, smoke colour or char colour baked in (the game adds fire and tint). Tone only from carving density.\n• Standing props (candles, holder, paper, cloth bundle, matchbox, match, lamp, ash piles) sit with their lowest ink on the ground line at 92% of the frame height, centred horizontally. Candles/holder: ground y=471 (512 tall) / 235.5 (256 tall); paper 478.4; cloth_bundle 644; lamp 588.8; matchbox 110.4; match 220.8; ash 184.\n• burn_candle_whole/half/stub: one cylinder family, same diameter and carving (vertical cut lines closer at the edges); half has its drip down the right side only; stub is melted low into a wide wax puddle with a bent wick. Wick tip is the flame anchor (top centre of each candle).\n• burn_candle_holder: a tin chamberstick (shallow dish, socket tube, ring handle to the right); the socket mouth centre is at (108, 137), left of frame centre because the ring handle is on the right; the whole piece is centred on the frame.\n• burn_paper_flat: a sheet standing on its edge in a slight 3/4 turn, a centre fold and a dog-eared corner, writing as wavy cut lines; burn_paper_curled: same sheet with the top rolled into a curl and the lower corner folded.\n• burn_cloth_line: a rag folded over a cord, folds as carved lines, ragged lower hem, a small hole; the cord runs nearly edge to edge (stops 6 px short of the frame so it does not touch the border) and dips under the rag's weight. It hangs in the air: no ground contact (lowest ink y=570). burn_cloth_bundle: a trouxa (cloth bundle) knotted at the top, printed with a small cut-out flower pattern.\n• burn_matchbox: a box with the drawer slid out at the right, star label; burn_match: an unstruck match standing upright, head at the top (flame anchor ~x=20, y=26). Small frames use HEAVY-based widths (cut lines ~1.7 px) because FINE would be under 1 px.\n• burn_lamp: a table kerosene lamp (candeeiro): stepped foot, round reservoir with a carved diamond band, burner gallery with a wick knob at the right, glass chimney as outline only (interior transparent). Flame anchor: wick top at (180, 263) inside the chimney; chimney mouth (smoke/heat) at (180, 33). FINE floored to 1.6 px.\n• burn_ash_1..3: low ash piles, mostly carved so ash reads light; a few ember dots cut out; _2 has a half-burnt stick in it, _3 is the flattest, widest spread.\n• burn_char_1..3: flat scorch decals seen from above at a slight slant, ragged spiky edges, alligator-crack carving and a few flecks around; _2 has flame tongues trailing right, _3 is a double mark with a burnt-through hole.\n• burn_scorch_1..2: a burnt circle of ground at a slant (ellipse), solid char ring with radial scorch rays at the edge and a lighter, carved ash centre (with charred sticks in _1). Centre of the ellipse is the anchor for a campfire/fire sprite (~x=384, y=156).\n• burn_ember_1..3: tiny 64x64 ember pieces (a faceted coal with a forked crack, a charred twig end, a pitted cinder with a fleck) for particles; centred.\n• burn_soot_1..2: vertical soot streak on a wall: dense at the bottom (the source, narrowing to a point at the base) fanning up into broken, rising wisps; place the base just above the fire/lamp. Wall decals, no ground line.\n• Reviewer: all 24 assets present at exact sizes; only change made was insetting the clothesline ends off the 2 px border. Nothing missing.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
