        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s9qxxxx",
          "x": 84,
          "y": 3248,
          "name": "Notes",
          "fill": "$ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 4336,
          "content": "• All animals are the existing design.pen figures (prop_onca, prop_tamandua, prop_capivara, prop_lobo_guara, prop_jacare, prop_tatu, prop_arara, prop_tucano), cut into parts with penref and re-posed. All face right, solid Ink with the carving cut out.\n• 4-pose sheets: 1024x1024, 2x2 grid, read in order. Each sheet keeps one ground line in all four cells, set at the top-row ground of that animal's existing anim_*_walk sheet (y within the cell): onça 427, tamanduá 410, capivara 423, lobo 463, jacaré 400, tatu 435. Tucano and arara use 427, the same as the onça.\n• anim_jacare_swim: only the eyes and eye ridge, snout and back scutes show above water. The bottom edge is a flat waterline at cell y 400. The tail sways side to side, so it shortens and lengthens from pose to pose. Put the water surface layer over y >= 400 in each cell.\n• anim_capivara_swim: head and back above water with a flat waterline at cell y 423. The paddling shows as the body bobbing and tilting.\n• anim_tucano_fly: a flap cycle with wings up, mid, down, then folded in a glide. Head and bill stay at the same height. With the wing down, cell 3 reaches lower; that is the wing, not a drop in body height.\n• anim_arara_takeoff: perched on a cut stump, leans forward with wings opening, wings spread, then lifts off with feet just above the stump. The stump stays fixed in every cell as the anchor.\n• anim_onca_run: a bounding gallop (gathered, extended, airborne, landing). anim_tamandua_flee: a lumbering run with the head low and the tail flag streaming. anim_lobo_run: a long-legged maned-wolf run.\n• anim_tatu_curl: walking, head tucking, half-rolled, then a closed ball with the head shield and tail tucked in. The ball sits on the same ground line.\n• prop_arara_branch 600x700: the arara perched on a forked branch with leaves. The trunk foot is on the ground line (y 644), centred.\n• prop_snake_watch 500x500: a coiled snake with its head raised and looking right, belly scales cut. The coil base is on the ground line (y 460), centred. A generic non-venomous-looking snake, not hurt.\n• Nothing missing. All 10 assets are done. Path sizes: onça sheet about 69k chars (under the 70k sheet limit), the rest under 40k.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    },
