        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "s14qxxxp",
          "x": 84,
          "y": 2650,
          "name": "Notes",
          "fill": "$ink",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": 3920,
          "content": "• Shared canvas 1920x1080, horizon at y=648 (60%). Frame positions on it (top-left): back_house_wall (0,-2) so its bottom edge sits on the horizon; back_house_floor (0,648); back_serra (0,268) so its base sits on the horizon; back_arraial (0,648); back_canopy (0,0) on top of everything. Every frame keeps the 2 px transparent border, so a hairline of the scene behind shows at the horizon seam (wall/floor, serra/arraial).\n• back_composite (extra, reference only): the house scene (wall over floor) on the left half and the outdoor scene (serra, arraial, canopy on top) on the right half, split by a carved vertical line at x=960, painted in order with a 3 px halo so the layers read; it shows the horizons line up. Not a game asset; its path is ~68k chars.\n• back_house_wall 1920x650 OPAQUE: wattle-and-daub plaster with a stippled surface, an exposed wood frame (top beam with peg holes, posts, diagonal braces), carved cracks, two patches where the plaster has fallen off showing the lath, a skirting band; door opening (x≈330-600) and window opening (x≈1150-1450, y≈190-410) fully transparent so the scene behind shows through.\n• back_house_floor 1920x430 OPAQUE, tileable horizontally (no border on x): packed earth as rows of carved dots growing toward the viewer (like layer_ground / room_floor), broom-sweep arcs, dry cracks, pebbles, two worn patches of square clay tiles (lajotas) in perspective. Periodic worn-smooth clear zones (one sits at the seam) keep the tiling invisible.\n• back_arraial 1920x420 OPAQUE from the horizon down: packed sand as dot/dash rows densifying toward the viewer, two trails of bare footprints, short straws, a bonfire scorch ring (radial cuts) at the right; the middle third (x≈700-1200) left clear for the festival action.\n• back_serra 1920x380 transparent above: two distant highland masses with contour carving and smaller ridges, araucária crowns on top (the layer_far candelabra crown), stippled foothills; solid base on the bottom edge. Reading of 'light carving': sparse fine contour lines, so the range stays a dark, distant silhouette like layer_far.\n• back_canopy 1920x1080 transparent: near-foliage frame like layer_near: a trunk and banana leaves on the left, a trunk, hanging lianas and palmate (embaúba-like) leaves on the right, ferns and grass clumps, a solid ground band along the bottom; the middle is clear for the clearing.\n• Line weights from each frame's shorter side (HEAVY 1.2% S, MEDIUM 0.6%, FINE 0.3%). On back_serra (S=380) and back_arraial (S=420) FINE would be ~1.1-1.3 px, so MEDIUM (2.3-2.5 px) is the finest cut there (HEAVY-based widths); the wall, floor and canopy use FINE ~2-3.2 px.\n• Nothing from the S14 list is missing.",
          "lineHeight": 1.5,
          "fontFamily": "Inter",
          "fontSize": 20,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
